content.text:
    "mutexAmong": [
      "pr_approved"
    ],
    "mutexExcludeSelf": true,
    "notLatestVerdict": [
      "REQUEST_CHANGES",
      "BLOCK"
    ]
  },
  "localAction": "validate_pr",
  "limit": 1,
  "id": "revalidate-armed-green",
  "skipIfGreenCi": true
},
{
  "description": "GitHub PR: head with no CONCLUDED validation (checks 'none' — fresh push, no CI — or 'pending' — the dispatch bridge's waiting check runs; pushes fire no CI) -> dispatch the CI workflow on the head + ai_validating marker. OWNER RULE (2026-09-23, validation economy): validate ONCE per PR — the first green is the ticket to review; after it the ai_validated latch excludes the PR here, silent-update keeps it fresh (no re-validation on refresh), and the single pre-merge validation lives in validate-armed (post-approve, current head). Red heads repeat this rule only after a NEW push clears the red. chore:pin PRs (factory lockstep bumps) are exempt: the factory suite gates them before the cut, and the next real PR validates the pinned content via silent-update. DELIBERATELY author-agnostic (gh-757 review): validating external/vendor PRs is the sanctioned prerequisite for the owner-ruled external review flow (review-external-once needs checks green, and pushes fire no CI) and for the guest sticky-park contract — only the auto-REWORK arm is machine-author-gated (fail_validation), never the validation dispatch itself.",
  "source": "github",
  "query": {
    "type": "pr",
    "checks": [
      "none",
      "pending"
    ],
    "notLabels": [
      "ai_validating",
      "pr_approved",
      "chore:pin",
      "ai_validated"
    ],
    "notMergeState": "BEHIND",
    "draft": false
  },
  "localAction": "validate_pr",
  "limit": 1,
  "id": "validate-fresh"
},
{
  "description": "Post-dev dead-zone fix (gh-759, live fa 2026-10-06: PRs #1305/#1306/#1309/#1311/#1312 — five fresh machine PRs BLOCKED with ZERO labels for hours, each unblocked by hand-arming ai_validating + dispatching CI; agents #756 / fa #1295 / fa #1304 are the same class patched by hand the same day). The dev leg completes (issue ai_developed + status:In Review) and the fresh head IMMEDIATELY carries GREEN check runs from the deployment's ambient workflows (fa: kicker sm-liveness/head-completeness, CodeQL, the analyze suite) — while the DISPATCH-ONLY validation CI (jobParams.ciWorkflow, no push trigger) has never been ordered. The rollup reads 'green', so validate-fresh (checks [none, pending]) never matches; every verdict/re-dispatch rule needs ai_validating or pr_approved, and the PR carries zero labels — nothing ever arms validation and the PR dead-locks BLOCKED. This rule is the UN-ARMED twin of revalidate-armed-green (gh-922): rollup green + BLOCKED + none of ai_validating/pr_approved/ai_validated/chore:pin/validation_failed → validate_pr probes the head for a dispatched CI run — none (or cancelled-only) → dispatch + arm ai_validating; a completed GREEN run → skipIfGreenCi skips (the blocker is another workflow's required check — re-running loops forever). Disjoint from validate-fresh by construction (none/pending vs green) and from every verdict rule by labels; notMergeState excludes BEHIND (silent-update refreshes first), DIRTY (conflict-rework) and CLEAN (merge-validated). Deliberately author-agnostic (gh-757 review): a guest PR's kicker-masked head is equally stranded, and validating external PRs is the sanctioned prerequisite for the external review flow — only the auto-REWORK arm is machine-gated, never the validation dispatch. Runs immediately AFTER validate-fresh, same dev-lane pacing (limit 1, no mutex — the merge window's mutexAmong [pr_approved] is untouched). Green verdicts flow through validated-green exactly as validate-fresh's do; red verdicts converge through sweep-stale-validating (which probes the dispatched run, not the masked rollup) into the standard fail path.",
  "source": "github",
  "query": {
    "type": "pr",
    "checks": "green",
    "notLabels": [
      "ai_validating",
      "pr_approved",
      "ai_validated",
      "chore:pin",
      "validation_failed"
    ],
    "notMergeState": [
      "BEHIND",
      "DIRTY",
      "CLEAN"
    ],
    "draft": false
  },
  "localAction": "validate_pr",
  "skipIfGreenCi": true,
  "limit": 1,
  "id": "validate-fresh-masked-green"
},
{
  "description": "GitHub PR: validation green but not yet approved -> latch ai_validated, unarm ai_validating. review-after-dev requires the latch + green checks, so review fires exactly once per validated head. Approved PRs are excluded (merge-validated / unarm-stale own them). Limit 10 (owner 2026-09-22): latch/unlatch verdicts in waves — pure label writes, nothing serial.",
  "source": "github",
  "query": {
    "type": "pr",
    "labels": [
      "ai_validating"
    ],
    "notLabels": [
      "pr_approved"
    ],
    "checks": "green"
  },
  "localAction": "complete_validation",
  "limit": 10,
  "id": "validated-green"
},
{
  "description": "GitHub PR: branch conflicts with main (silent-update's git merge cannot land; mergeState DIRTY) -> the queue would stall forever — report and, for MACHINE-authored PRs, re-arm agent:rework on the linked issue so the agent resolves the conflicts and pushes; the normal validate flow then resumes (pr_approved is STICKY — no re-review). Guest PRs get the report only (owner rule 2026-09-21: auto-rework is machine-author-only). Fires once per head: the marker comment carries the head sha and suppresses re-reports for the same head — never the arming (gh-683 bug C, live fa #677/#676 2026-10-03: the marker used to land before arming, a starved dispatch left a reported corpse and the issue was never labelled). Arming lands FIRST, the marker LAST; a marker whose linked issue lacks agent:rework re-arms on the next tick (suppression keys on the label, not the comment).",
  "source": "github",
  "query": {
    "type": "pr",
    "mergeState": [
      "DIRTY"
    ],
    "draft": false
  },
  "localAction": "conflict_rework",
  "limit": 1,
  "id": "conflict-rework"
